# Rust workspace

## Crates

- **`furnigen-core`**: `std` ok; deterministic geometry; **`serde`** for spec types. No `web_sys`, no Three.
- **`furnigen-wasm`**: thin **`wasm-bindgen`** surface calling core; minimize allocations on hot paths.

## Quality bar

- Run **`cargo fmt`** and **`cargo clippy`** (warnings as errors in CI when CI lands).
- Prefer **`thiserror`** (or similar) for recoverable validation errors; avoid stringly-typed errors across crate boundaries.
- Use **`Result`** for I/O and validation; reserve **`panic!`** for programmer bugs only.

## Numerics

- **`f32` vs `f64`**: pick one per module for geometry and stick to it; document if WASM ABI forces `f32`.
- Avoid silent unit mixing; name types or fields with **`_mm`** when ambiguity is possible.

## Tests

- **`cargo test`** on core: invariants (panel thickness, box dimensions, straight-run assumptions).
- Property tests are welcome for numeric ranges when they stay fast.

## Features

- Gate **`console_error_panic_hook`** and dev-only helpers behind **`cfg`** / features so release WASM stays small.
